WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.600
Count the commandments in the Torah,
and Jewish tradition finds 613 of them.

2
00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:11.600
In 1793, the philosopher Immanuel Kant
looked at them and saw political laws,

3
00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.600
not a moral religion.

4
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:19.300
Yet on duty and on human dignity, Kant
and Jewish teaching seem to agree.

5
00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:23.270
So is Jewish ethics really
about rules, about results,

6
00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:25.070
or about character?

7
00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:29.010
In this mission, you'll set Jewish
teaching beside three thinkers:

8
00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:31.760
Kant, Bentham and Aristotle.

9
00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:35.520
Then you'll build an argument
map on one bold claim:

10
00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:39.380
that Jewish ethics is best
described as duty-based.

11
00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.250
Your mission: weigh up whether
Jewish ethics is about rules,

12
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.010
results or character.
